{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>למען</b> (So that) — and the sense is: 'I will give thanks to You all my days, so that [others] give thanks to You.'" "<b>ויזמרך</b> (And sing to You) — every person who possesses honor. And the sense: a wise soul, and because the discerning are few." "He said: <b>כבוד</b> (honor) — and not all honor."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:00.604463859Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}